## Architecture & Patterns

### Traditional ETL Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   Source Systems                     │
│  (Databases, APIs, Files, CRM, ERP, Cloud Apps)    │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
         ┌───────▼────────┐
         │    EXTRACT     │
         │   (Read data)  │
         └───────┬────────┘
                 │
         ┌───────▼──────────────────────┐
         │   STAGING AREA               │
         │ (Temporary storage for raw)  │
         └───────┬──────────────────────┘
                 │
         ┌───────▼────────────────────────┐
         │    TRANSFORM                   │
         │  (Clean, Validate, Aggregate)  │
         │  (Business logic application)  │
         └───────┬────────────────────────┘
                 │
         ┌───────▼──────────────────────┐
         │   STAGING AREA (Cleaned)     │
         │ (Intermediate clean tables)  │
         └───────┬──────────────────────┘
                 │
         ┌───────▼────────┐
         │     LOAD       │
         │  (Write data)  │
         └───────┬────────┘
                 │
┌────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│             Target System                            │
│  (Data Warehouse, Data Lake, BI Platform)           │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Staging Area Concept

**Purpose of Staging:**
1. **Isolation**: Separate source systems from transformation logic
2. **Performance**: Optimize bulk operations
3. **Debugging**: Store intermediate results for troubleshooting
4. **Rollback**: Ability to restore from checkpoint

**Staging Layers:**
```
Layer 1: Raw Staging
├─ Exact copy of source data
├─ No transformations applied
└─ Used for backup and debugging

Layer 2: Cleaned Staging
├─ Data validation applied
├─ Basic transformations
├─ Duplicate removal
└─ Format standardization

Layer 3: Business Staging
├─ Business rules applied
├─ Aggregations and calculations
├─ Dimension tables
└─ Fact tables
```

